  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Agr 904.05 Color Standards",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-02-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 904.05 Color Standards.\n\n(a) Color standards with the equivalent results to the following light transmittance values (%Tc) on a spectrophotometer shall be as follows:\n\n(1) “Golden” ≥75.0;\n\n(2) “Amber” 50.0-74.9;\n\n(3) “Dark” 25.0-49.9; and\n\n(4) “Very Dark” <25.0.\n\n(b) A color comparator or digital color transmission spectrophotometer shall be used for determining the color grade of maple syrup.\n\nSource. #2656, eff 3-23-84, EXPIRED 3-23-90\n\nNew. #4956, eff 10-19-90; EXPIRED 10-19-96\n\nNew. #6453, eff 2-15-97, EXPIRED: 2-15-05\n\nNew. #10744, eff 12-16-14 (from Agr 904.04); ss by #14225, eff 3-29-25 (formerly Agr 904.04)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr900.html"
